IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- scja1-part3-div1.l4: Supreme Court of Judicature Act 1969 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 July 2024.
-- LAYER 1, Part 3 "General Division of High Court", Division 1 "General", ss 9 to 14 (s 9 and s 12 are shown repealed). The source is a plain-text rendering, not the official text.
-- Every name begins with the section it implements. Imports the keel's `scja-core` and the staged Interpretation Act time module (a Sunday, for s 10B), copied unchanged.
-- A judgment the text leaves to a Judge, the court or the Chief Justice is a plain input, never guessed.

§ `Part 3: General Division of High Court`

§§ `Division 1: General`

-- s 9 and s 12: "[Repealed by Act 40 of 2019]" -- nothing to encode (coverage table: repealed or blank in this text).

§§§ `Section 10: Proceedings in General Division`

-- s 10(1). Subject to (1A): every proceeding in the General Division is heard before a single Judge, or before any other number of Judges as provided by a written law.
-- src:771 | 10.—(1) Subject to subsection (1A), every proceeding in the
-- src:772 | General Division and all business arising out of the proceeding is
-- src:773 | to be heard and disposed of before a single Judge, or before any other
-- src:774 | number of Judges as provided by any written law for the time being in
-- src:775 | force.
@ref s 10(1) (src:771-775)
GIVEN `the number of Judges any written law provides for this proceeding` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc If a written law provides that the proceeding is heard before a number of Judges other than one, how many? Leave blank if none does.
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 10(1) the number of Judges before whom the proceeding is heard and disposed of` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of Judges any written law provides for this proceeding`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN 1
    WHEN JUST n THEN n

-- s 10(1A). Despite (1): the Chief Justice may direct that a proceeding be heard before any uneven number of Judges greater than the number under (1). The grant is limited by its own
-- wording ("any uneven number ... greater than"): a number that is even, or not greater, is outside it and the section is silent (NOTHING).
-- src:779 | (1A) Despite subsection (1) and any other written law mentioned in
-- src:780 | that subsection, the Chief Justice may direct that any particular
-- src:781 | proceeding in the General Division be heard before a court consisting
-- src:782 | of any uneven number of Judges greater than the number provided
-- src:783 | under subsection (1) or that other written law.
@ref s 10(1A) (src:779-783)
GIVEN `the number of Judges directed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Judges does the direction ask for?
      `the number of Judges under section 10(1)` IS A NUMBER @desc How many Judges would hear the proceeding without the direction (one, unless a written law provides another number)?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(1A) the Chief Justice may direct that the proceeding be heard before this number of Judges` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the number of Judges directed` MODULO 2 EQUALS 1 AND `the number of Judges directed` GREATER THAN `the number of Judges under section 10(1)` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any uneven number of Judges greater than the number provided under subsection (1)"

-- How a proceeding before 3 or more Judges is decided (s 10(1B)).
DECLARE `s 10(1B) decision` IS ONE OF
    `s 10(1B) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, for the claim, appeal or application`
    `s 10(1B) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, against the claim, appeal or application`
    `s 10(1B) not covered`

-- s 10(1B). A proceeding before 3 or more Judges must be decided in accordance with the opinion of the majority of them. Fewer than 3 Judges, or an even split: the section does not say.
-- src:787 | (1B) A proceeding in the General Division before 3 or more Judges
-- src:788 | must be decided in accordance with the opinion of the majority of
-- src:789 | them.
@ref s 10(1B) (src:787-789)
GIVEN split IS A `Split of opinion`
GIVETH A `s 10(1B) decision`
`s 10(1B) how a proceeding before 3 or more Judges is decided` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF split's `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` PLUS split's `Judges against it` LESS THAN 3 THEN `s 10(1B) not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A proceeding in the General Division before 3 or more Judges"
        IF split's `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` GREATER THAN split's `Judges against it` THEN `s 10(1B) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, for the claim, appeal or application`
        IF split's `Judges for the claim, appeal or application` LESS THAN split's `Judges against it` THEN `s 10(1B) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, against the claim, appeal or application`
        OTHERWISE `s 10(1B) not covered` -- NOTHING-kind (silent): no majority when the Judges divide evenly

-- s 10(2). A Judge may, subject to Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules, exercise in court or in chambers all or any part of the General Division's jurisdiction in the causes and matters
-- a single Judge could have heard immediately before 9 January 1970, or that the Rules direct or authorise a Judge to hear.
-- src:793 | (2) A Judge may, subject to Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules,
-- src:794 | exercise in court or in chambers all or any part of the jurisdiction
-- src:795 | vested in the General Division, in all such causes and matters and in
-- src:796 | all such proceedings in any causes or matters as might immediately
-- src:797 | before 9 January 1970 have been heard in court or in chambers
-- src:798 | respectively by a single Judge, or as may be directed or authorised to
-- src:799 | be so heard by Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules for the time
-- src:800 | being in force.
@ref s 10(2) (src:793-800)
GIVEN `a single Judge could have heard it immediately before 9 January 1970` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Could a single Judge, in court or in chambers, have heard this kind of cause, matter or proceeding immediately before 9 January 1970?
      `the Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules direct or authorise it to be heard by a Judge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules direct or authorise this kind of cause, matter or proceeding to be heard by a Judge in court or in chambers?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(2) a Judge may exercise the jurisdiction of the General Division in the cause, matter or proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a single Judge could have heard it immediately before 9 January 1970` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules direct or authorise it to be heard by a Judge` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in all such causes and matters ... as might immediately before 9 January 1970 have been heard ... or as may be directed or authorised ... by Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules"

-- s 10(3): "[Deleted by Act 42 of 2014]" -- nothing to encode.

-- s 10(4). A Judge who reserves judgment, and whose appointment expires or is terminated before delivering it, has power to deliver it.
-- src:806 | (4) If a Judge reserves judgment in any proceedings and his or her
-- src:807 | appointment as a Judge expires or is terminated before his or her
-- src:808 | judgment is delivered, he or she has power to deliver judgment in
-- src:809 | respect of those proceedings, even though his or her appointment as a
-- src:810 | Judge has expired or has been terminated.
@ref s 10(4) (src:806-810)
GIVEN `the Judge reserved judgment in the proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Judge reserve judgment in the proceedings?
      `the Judge's appointment expired or was terminated before judgment was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Judge's appointment as a Judge expire or get terminated before the judgment was delivered?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(4) the Judge has power to deliver judgment despite the expiry or termination of the appointment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Judge reserved judgment in the proceedings` AND `the Judge's appointment expired or was terminated before judgment was delivered` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a Judge reserves judgment in any proceedings and his or her appointment as a Judge expires or is terminated before his or her judgment is delivered"

-- The proceedings s 10(5) names, each connected with the Judge acting as the Presiding Judge of the State Courts or of the Family Justice Courts.
DECLARE `s 10(5) proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `s 10(5)(a) an appeal from a judgment or order made by the Judge as the Presiding Judge`
    `s 10(5)(b) an appeal against a conviction before, or a sentence passed by, the Judge as the Presiding Judge`
    `s 10(5)(c) the consideration of a case stated by the Judge under section 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 as the Presiding Judge`
    `s 10(5)(d) an application under section 400 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 in relation to a judgment, order or sentence by the Judge as the Presiding Judge`
    `s 10(5)(e) any proceedings relating to any judgment, order or direction made by the Judge as the Presiding Judge`
    `s 10(5) another proceeding`

-- s 10(5). Plain gloss: must this Judge not sit on the hearing of, or determine an application in proceedings incidental or preliminary to, one of (a) to (e)?
-- A flat negative on the Judge who acted as the Presiding Judge; a Judge who did not so act, or proceedings outside (a) to (e), are outside its wording.
-- src:817 | (5) No Judge is to sit in the General Division on the hearing of, or
-- src:818 | determine any application in proceedings incidental or preliminary
-- src:819 | to —
-- src:821 | (a) an appeal from a judgment or an order made by the Judge
-- src:822 | as the Presiding Judge of the State Courts or the Presiding
-- src:823 | Judge of the Family Justice Courts;
-- src:825 | (b) an appeal against a conviction before the Judge or a
-- src:826 | sentence passed by the Judge as the Presiding Judge of the
-- src:827 | State Courts or the Presiding Judge of the Family Justice
-- src:828 | Courts;
-- src:830 | (c) the consideration of any case stated by the Judge under
-- src:831 | section 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010 as the
-- src:832 | Presiding Judge of the State Courts or the Presiding Judge
-- src:833 | of the Family Justice Courts;
-- src:835 | (d) any application made under section 400 of the Criminal
-- src:836 | Procedure Code 2010 in relation to any judgment or order
-- src:837 | made, or sentence passed, by the Judge as the Presiding
-- src:838 | Judge of the State Courts or the Presiding Judge of the
-- src:839 | Family Justice Courts; or
-- src:841 | (e) any proceedings relating to any judgment, order or
-- src:842 | direction made by the Judge as the Presiding Judge of
-- src:843 | the State Courts or the Presiding Judge of the Family
-- src:844 | Justice Courts.
@ref s 10(5) (src:817-844)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `s 10(5) proceeding` @desc Which proceeding is it: (a) an appeal from the Presiding Judge's judgment or order; (b) an appeal against conviction or sentence by the Presiding Judge; (c) a case stated under s 395 of the Criminal Procedure Code 2010; (d) an application under s 400 of that Code; (e) any proceedings relating to the Presiding Judge's judgment, order or direction; or another?
      `this Judge is the Judge who acted as the Presiding Judge of the State Courts or of the Family Justice Courts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the Judge in question the Judge who made the judgment, order, direction or sentence as the Presiding Judge of the State Courts or the Presiding Judge of the Family Justice Courts?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) the Judge must not sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF proceeding EQUALS `s 10(5) another proceeding` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings incidental or preliminary to" (a) to (e)
        IF `this Judge is the Judge who acted as the Presiding Judge of the State Courts or of the Family Justice Courts` THEN JUST TRUE -- the bar applies: "No Judge is to sit in the General Division on the hearing of, or determine any application in proceedings incidental or preliminary to" (a) to (e)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (a) to (e) each speak of what "the Judge" did "as the Presiding Judge"

-- s 10(5), the twin for the grant: may this Judge sit? JUST TRUE answers the bar above, so this twin is JUST FALSE where the bar applies and NOTHING elsewhere (the section says nothing of a Judge outside it).
@ref s 10(5) the Judge may sit (src:817-844)
GIVEN proceeding IS A `s 10(5) proceeding`
      `this Judge is the Judge who acted as the Presiding Judge of the State Courts or of the Family Justice Courts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10(5) the Judge may sit in the General Division on the hearing or determine an application in the proceeding` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF proceeding EQUALS `s 10(5) another proceeding` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "proceedings incidental or preliminary to" (a) to (e)
        IF `this Judge is the Judge who acted as the Presiding Judge of the State Courts or of the Family Justice Courts` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "No Judge is to sit in the General Division on the hearing of, or determine any application in proceedings incidental or preliminary to" (a) to (e)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): (a) to (e) each speak of what "the Judge" did "as the Presiding Judge"

§§§ `Section 10A: Assessors to assist General Division`

-- s 10A(1). Seam 13 of PLAN.md: ss 32(3) and 50(3) (scja2) make s 10A apply to the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal; the court is therefore an input.
-- "if it thinks fit, on the application of any party, or on its own motion": the court's judgment is a plain input. The Singapore International Commercial Court is not named (K1).
-- src:852 | 10A.—(1) In any proceedings before the General Division, the
-- src:853 | Court may, if it thinks fit on the application of any party, or on its own
-- src:854 | motion, summon to its assistance, in such manner as may be
-- src:855 | prescribed by Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules, one or more
-- src:856 | persons of skill and experience in the matter to which the proceedings
-- src:857 | relate who may be willing to sit with the Court and act as assessors.
@ref s 10A(1) (src:852-857)
GIVEN court IS A Court
      `the court thinks fit to summon assessors` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court think fit, on a party's application or on its own motion, to summon to its assistance one or more persons of skill and experience in the matter, to sit with it as assessors?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10A the court may summon assessors` MEANS
    CONSIDER court
    WHEN `General Division` THEN
        IF `the court thinks fit to summon assessors` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it thinks fit"
    WHEN `Appellate Division` THEN
        IF `the court thinks fit to summon assessors` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it thinks fit" (reached through s 32(3))
    WHEN `Court of Appeal` THEN
        IF `the court thinks fit to summon assessors` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if it thinks fit" (reached through s 50(3))
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In any proceedings before the General Division"; the Singapore International Commercial Court is a division of it (s 18A) but s 10A does not say so (K1)

-- s 10A(2) and (3). Remuneration of assessors: costs in the proceedings unless the General Division orders otherwise; where the assessors are not summoned on a party's application,
-- payable out of moneys provided by Parliament. The rate is prescribed by Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules (outside the sources).
-- src:861 | (2) Subject to subsection (3), the remuneration of assessors for
-- src:862 | sitting under this section is to be at such rate as may be prescribed by
-- src:869 | Rules of Court or Family Justice Rules and is to be costs in the
-- src:870 | proceedings unless otherwise ordered by the General Division.
-- src:874 | (3) Where one or more assessors are summoned for the purposes of
-- src:875 | this section otherwise than on the application of a party to the
-- src:876 | proceedings, the remuneration of any such assessor is payable out of
-- src:877 | moneys provided by Parliament.
@ref s 10A(2), (3) (src:861-877)
GIVEN `the assessors were summoned on the application of a party` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were the assessors summoned on the application of a party to the proceedings?
      `the General Division has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the General Division ordered that the remuneration is not to be costs in the proceedings?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10A(2) the remuneration of the assessors is costs in the proceedings` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the assessors were summoned on the application of a party` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to subsection (3)": where the assessors are not summoned on a party's application, subsection (3) governs
        IF `the General Division has otherwise ordered` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless otherwise ordered by the General Division"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 10A(3) (src:874-877)
GIVEN `the assessors were summoned on the application of a party` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10A(3) the remuneration of the assessors is payable out of moneys provided by Parliament` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the assessors were summoned on the application of a party` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where one or more assessors are summoned for the purposes of this section otherwise than on the application of a party"

-- s 10A(4). Where a person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor, a party may object to the person, personally or as to qualification, in the prescribed manner.
-- src:879 | (4) Where any person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor,
-- src:880 | objection to the person, either personally or in respect of the person’s
-- src:881 | qualification, may be taken by any party in the prescribed manner.
@ref s 10A(4) (src:879-881)
GIVEN `a person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is a person proposed to be summoned as an assessor?
      `the objection is to the person or to the person's qualification` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the objection to the person, personally, or to the person's qualification?
      `the party objects in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you object in the manner prescribed by the Rules of Court or the Family Justice Rules?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10A(4) a party may take objection to the proposed assessor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `a person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where any person is proposed to be summoned as an assessor"
        IF `the objection is to the person or to the person's qualification` AND `the party objects in the prescribed manner` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "either personally or in respect of the person's qualification ... in the prescribed manner"

§§§ `Section 10B: When General Division is open`

-- A Saturday, found from the Interpretation Act module's Sunday (the day before a Sunday).
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 10B(1) the day is a Saturday` d MEANS
    `is a Sunday` (d PLUS 1)

-- s 10B(1). Subject to (2): the General Division is to sit on every day of the year except Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays. The public holidays are a fact asked of the person.
-- src:885 | 10B.—(1) Subject to subsection (2), the General Division is to sit
-- src:886 | on every day of the year except on Saturdays, Sundays and public
-- src:887 | holidays.
@ref s 10B(1) (src:885-887)
GIVEN day IS A DATE @desc For which date are you asking?
      `the public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE @desc Which dates in the year are public holidays? List them, or leave empty if none.
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10B(1) the General Division is to sit on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 10B(1) the day is a Saturday` day THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays"
        IF `is a Sunday` day THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays"
        IF elem day `the public holidays` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 10B(2). Despite (1), a Judge may lawfully sit on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday, or during a vacation prescribed under s 7, if (a) the Chief Justice has directed the Judge to sit that day,
-- or (b) in the Judge's opinion the business to be despatched is extremely urgent. A day that is none of those: the subsection does not speak of it.
-- src:891 | (2) Despite subsection (1), a Judge may lawfully sit on a Saturday,
-- src:892 | Sunday or public holiday or during a vacation prescribed under
-- src:893 | section 7 if —
-- src:895 | (a) the Chief Justice has directed the Judge to sit on that day or
-- src:896 | during that vacation; or
-- src:898 | (b) in the opinion of the Judge, the business to be despatched is
-- src:899 | extremely urgent.
@ref s 10B(2) (src:891-899)
GIVEN `the day is a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday or falls in a vacation prescribed under section 7` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the day a Saturday, a Sunday, a public holiday, or a day in a vacation of the Supreme Court?
      `the Chief Justice has directed the Judge to sit on that day or during that vacation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Chief Justice directed the Judge to sit on that day or during that vacation?
      `in the opinion of the Judge the business to be despatched is extremely urgent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc In the Judge's opinion, is the business to be despatched extremely urgent?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 10B(2) the Judge may lawfully sit on the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the day is a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday or falls in a vacation prescribed under section 7` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday or during a vacation prescribed under section 7"
        IF `the Chief Justice has directed the Judge to sit on that day or during that vacation` THEN JUST TRUE -- (a)
        IF `in the opinion of the Judge the business to be despatched is extremely urgent` THEN JUST TRUE -- (b)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if (a) ... or (b)"

§§§ `Section 11: Sittings of General Division and distribution of business`

-- s 11(1). The General Division sits at the times and places the Chief Justice appoints.
-- src:905 | 11.—(1) The General Division is to sit at such times and at such
-- src:906 | places as the Chief Justice may from time to time appoint.
@ref s 11(1) (src:905-906)
GIVEN `the Chief Justice has appointed the time and place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the Chief Justice appointed this time and this place for the General Division to sit?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(1) the General Division sits at the time and place` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Chief Justice has appointed the time and place` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "at such times and at such places as the Chief Justice may from time to time appoint"

-- s 11(2). The distribution of business among the Judges is made in accordance with the Chief Justice's directions, general or particular. A bare "is to be" not done answers NOTHING: the text states a duty and does not say what follows (question QB; fork F7).
-- src:910 | (2) The distribution of business among the several Judges is to be
-- src:911 | made in accordance with such directions, which may be of a general
-- src:912 | or a particular nature, as may be given by the Chief Justice.
@ref s 11(2) (src:910-912)
GIVEN `the distribution is made in accordance with the directions of the Chief Justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the distribution of business among the Judges made in accordance with the Chief Justice's directions?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 11(2) the distribution of business among the Judges is as the Act requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the distribution is made in accordance with the directions of the Chief Justice` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "is to be made in accordance with such directions" states a duty and does not say what follows if the distribution is made otherwise (fork F7)

§§§ `Section 13: Enforcement orders for seizure and sale of property`

-- The kinds of property s 13 sorts: the five exceptions, and property of any other description.
DECLARE `s 13 property` IS ONE OF
    `s 13(a) wearing apparel and bedding of the judgment debtor or the judgment debtor's family, and the tools and implements of the judgment debtor's trade`
    `s 13(b) tools of artisans`
    `s 13(b) an agriculturist's implements of husbandry, and such animals and seed-grain or produce as are necessary to earn a livelihood`
    `s 13(c) the wages or salary of the judgment debtor`
    `s 13(d) a pension, gratuity or allowance granted by the Government`
    `s 13(e) the share of the judgment debtor in a partnership`
    `s 13 property of any other description`

-- s 13. Plain gloss: may this property of a judgment debtor be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale? A money judgment may be enforced against all property "except" (a) to (e).
-- (a) only "when the value ... does not exceed $1,000"; (b) animals and produce "as may in the opinion of the court be necessary"; (e) where the creditor is entitled to proceed to obtain a charge under a written law.
-- The exceptions are closed by "except": property outside them may be seized.
-- src:923 | 13. A judgment for the payment of money to any person or into
-- src:924 | court may be enforced by an enforcement order for seizure and sale of
-- src:925 | property, under which all the property, movable or immovable, of
-- src:926 | whatever description, of a judgment debtor may be seized, except —
-- src:928 | (a) the wearing apparel and bedding of the judgment debtor or
-- src:929 | the judgment debtor’s family, and the tools and implements
-- src:930 | of the judgment debtor’s trade, when the value of such
-- src:931 | apparel, bedding, tools and implements does not exceed
-- src:932 | $1,000;
-- src:934 | (b) tools of artisans, and, where the judgment debtor is an
-- src:935 | agriculturist, the judgment debtor’s implements of
-- src:936 | husbandry and such animals and seed‑grain or produce
-- src:937 | as may in the opinion of the court be necessary to enable
-- src:938 | the judgment debtor to earn his or her livelihood as such;
-- src:940 | (c) the wages or salary of the judgment debtor;
-- src:942 | (d) any pension, gratuity or allowance granted by the
-- src:943 | Government; and
-- src:945 | (e) the share of the judgment debtor in a partnership, as to
-- src:946 | which the judgment creditor is entitled to proceed to obtain
-- src:947 | a charge under any provision of any written law relating to
-- src:948 | partnership.
@ref s 13 (src:923-948)
GIVEN `the judgment is for the payment of money to any person or into court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment one for the payment of money to any person or into court?
      property IS A `s 13 property` @desc Which property: (a) clothes, bedding and tools of trade; (b) tools of artisans, or an agriculturist's implements, animals and produce; (c) wages or salary; (d) a Government pension, gratuity or allowance; (e) a partnership share; or any other property?
      `the value of the apparel, bedding, tools and implements in (a)` IS A NUMBER @desc For clothes, bedding, tools and implements of trade: what is their total value in dollars? (0 if not applicable)
      `in the opinion of the court the animals, seed-grain or produce are necessary to earn the livelihood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the court consider the agriculturist's animals, seed-grain or produce necessary to enable the judgment debtor to earn a livelihood as an agriculturist?
      `the judgment creditor is entitled to proceed to obtain a charge on the share under a written law relating to partnership` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment creditor entitled to proceed to obtain a charge on the share under a written law relating to partnership?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 the property of the judgment debtor may be seized under an enforcement order for seizure and sale` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the judgment is for the payment of money to any person or into court` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A judgment for the payment of money to any person or into court may be enforced"
        IF property EQUALS `s 13(a) wearing apparel and bedding of the judgment debtor or the judgment debtor's family, and the tools and implements of the judgment debtor's trade`
           AND `the value of the apparel, bedding, tools and implements in (a)` AT MOST 1000 THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except (a) ... when the value of such apparel, bedding, tools and implements does not exceed $1,000"
        IF property EQUALS `s 13(b) tools of artisans` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... (b) tools of artisans"
        IF property EQUALS `s 13(b) an agriculturist's implements of husbandry, and such animals and seed-grain or produce as are necessary to earn a livelihood`
           AND `in the opinion of the court the animals, seed-grain or produce are necessary to earn the livelihood` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... (b) ... such animals and seed-grain or produce as may in the opinion of the court be necessary"
        IF property EQUALS `s 13(c) the wages or salary of the judgment debtor` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... (c) the wages or salary of the judgment debtor"
        IF property EQUALS `s 13(d) a pension, gratuity or allowance granted by the Government` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... (d) any pension, gratuity or allowance granted by the Government"
        IF property EQUALS `s 13(e) the share of the judgment debtor in a partnership`
           AND `the judgment creditor is entitled to proceed to obtain a charge on the share under a written law relating to partnership` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except ... (e) the share of the judgment debtor in a partnership, as to which the judgment creditor is entitled to proceed to obtain a charge"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- the list of exceptions is closed by "except": "all the property, movable or immovable, of whatever description, of a judgment debtor may be seized"

§§§ `Section 14: Execution of deed or indorsement of negotiable instrument`

-- s 14(1)(a), (b) and (c), (d). Plain gloss: may an interested party prepare the deed, document or indorsement and tender it to the court for execution? Only if (a) the judgment or order is for the execution of a deed,
-- signing of a document or indorsement of a negotiable instrument and (b) the party ordered is absent, or neglects or refuses to do so.
-- src:956 | 14.—(1) If —
-- src:958 | (a) a judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, or
-- src:959 | signing of a document, or for the indorsement of a
-- src:960 | negotiable instrument; and
-- src:962 | (b) the party ordered to execute, sign or indorse such
-- src:963 | instrument is absent, or neglects or refuses to do so,
-- src:965 | any party interested in having the same executed, signed or indorsed,
-- src:966 | may —
@ref s 14(1) (src:956-966)
GIVEN `the judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the judgment or order for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document, or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument?
      `the party ordered is absent, or neglects or refuses to do it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the party ordered to execute, sign or indorse it absent, or neglecting or refusing to do so?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) the interested party may prepare the instrument and tender it to the court for execution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument` AND `the party ordered is absent, or neglects or refuses to do it` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If (a) ... and (b) ..."

-- s 14(1), last limb. The Registrar's signature, by order of the court, on the instrument prepared in accordance with the judgment or order (c) and tendered upon the proper stamp (d), has the same effect as execution by the party ordered.
-- src:973 | (c) prepare a deed, or document, or indorsement of the
-- src:974 | instrument in accordance with the terms of the judgment
-- src:975 | or order; and
-- src:977 | (d) tender the same to the court for execution upon the proper
-- src:978 | stamp, if any is required by law,
-- src:980 | and the signature thereof by the Registrar, by order of the court, has
-- src:981 | the same effect as the execution, signing or indorsement thereof by
-- src:982 | the party ordered to execute.
@ref s 14(1)(c), (d) and the closing words (src:973-982)
GIVEN `the judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the party ordered is absent, or neglects or refuses to do it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument was prepared in accordance with the terms of the judgment or order` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was the deed, document or indorsement prepared in accordance with the terms of the judgment or order?
      `it was tendered to the court for execution upon the proper stamp, if any is required by law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was it tendered to the court for execution upon the proper stamp, if any is required by law?
      `the Registrar signed it by order of the court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did the Registrar sign it by order of the court?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(1) the Registrar's signature has the same effect as execution by the party ordered` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 14(1) the interested party may prepare the instrument and tender it to the court for execution` `the judgment or order is for the execution of a deed, the signing of a document or the indorsement of a negotiable instrument` `the party ordered is absent, or neglects or refuses to do it` EQUALS JUST TRUE
           AND `the instrument was prepared in accordance with the terms of the judgment or order`
           AND `it was tendered to the court for execution upon the proper stamp, if any is required by law`
           AND `the Registrar signed it by order of the court` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If (a) ... and (b) ..." with steps (c) and (d) and "the signature thereof by the Registrar, by order of the court"

-- s 14(2). Nothing in s 14 abridges the court's power to proceed by attachment against a person neglecting or refusing to execute, sign or indorse. A flat negative; the person who is not so neglecting is outside it.
-- src:984 | (2) Nothing in this section is to be held to abridge the powers of the
-- src:985 | court to proceed by attachment against any person neglecting or
-- src:986 | refusing to execute, sign or indorse any such instrument.
@ref s 14(2) (src:984-986)
GIVEN `the person is neglecting or refusing to execute, sign or indorse the instrument` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the person neglecting or refusing to execute, sign or indorse the instrument?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14(2) section 14 abridges the court's power to proceed by attachment against the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the person is neglecting or refusing to execute, sign or indorse the instrument` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section is to be held to abridge the powers of the court to proceed by attachment"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "against any person neglecting or refusing to execute, sign or indorse any such instrument"
